+# V4 common retained-cache idle correction
+
+Scope: common baseline correction, applied identically to off, shadow, and on.
+This correction is not an interference-policy improvement or a GPU result.
+
+## Observed source defect
+
+The original `_has_work()` includes retained `_shared_cached` and
+`_preload_slots`. `_run()` used that ownership predicate to choose whether the
+existing incoming queue may block. Consequently retained cache alone repeatedly
+entered the original pump and its `time.sleep(0)` path, even with no operation
+to poll or advance. The historical GPU timing pattern motivated this correction
+but does not by itself establish its causal performance effect.
+
+## Exact change
+
+Add `_has_poll_work()` and use it only for the existing
+`_drain_incoming(block=...)` argument in `_run()`.
+
+The new predicate remains true for STOP, active parents, ring operations,
+pending CUDA copies, ready copies, pending preload work, and both original
+ready-fd queues. It ignores only retained cache ownership. It does not scan,
+evict, copy, release, or change any resource. In particular, an actively deferred
+ready preload remains polling work; this correction does not resolve its retry
+cost.
+
+`_has_work`, `_pump_once`, `_drain_incoming`, `_intake`, `shutdown`, and the normal
+STOP cleanup are unchanged. The original `Queue.get(timeout=0.5)` and all original
+submission channels remain in use. No new queue, event, sleep parameter, model
+change, or lifecycle protocol is introduced. Arrival between the predicate
+check and `get()` remains safe because the original Queue owns its wakeup.
+
+## CPU evidence and limits
+
+Local isolated Python 3.12 execution on 2026-10-03:
+
+```text
+python -B -I -S test_retained_idle_wait.py
+Ran 15 tests in 0.170s
+OK
+```
+
+The suite extracts actual reactor run/intake/submission/STOP methods by AST,
+uses real `queue.Queue` and Python threads, and checks the old source against
+v3. It covers shared and nonshared retained caches, each polling-work category,
+job/preload/mandatory/owner-snapshot/P4-inspect/P4-publication/admission-control
+wakeups, FIFO job-before-mandatory ordering, check-to-get arrival races, STOP
+wakeup and exactly-once retained-slot release.
+
+The model, CUDA, ring backend, and pump completion work are explicit CPU
+fixtures. Source comparisons prove the original actual pump and STOP code were
+not changed; these tests do not prove real DMA completion or GPU performance.
+The suite asserts Torch/vLLM are not imported. There were no GPU operations,
+remote commands, deletion, or changes to older candidate versions.
+
+For a server artifact directory with a different name, set
+`SERVER11_IDLE_PREVIOUS_CANDIDATE_DIR` to the actual immutable v3 candidate root
+before invoking this test. Old copied structural-regression tests also need
+their explicit allowed-change lists updated by the candidate integrator; this
+task does not edit those tests or the unified candidate manifest.
+
+## Fairness and cost evidence
+
+All comparison arms must share this correction and the same initial cache,
+budgets, engine, lifecycle, and measurements. New-on versus historical-off is
+not a strategy comparison. The correction can change I/O-window CPU competition;
+the previous v5 cost calibration remains historical evidence and must not be
+silently promoted to qualification for the corrected common baseline. A future
+qualification needs source-bound calibration and held-out validation, with no
+widening of prior thresholds to conceal a regression.
